@host = http://localhost:5000

# Creates the 4 shop products from mockData/products.json. Run it ONCE (running it twice makes 8 products).
#
# BEFORE YOU START:
#   1. Run test A in auth.http (it saves adminToken). Access tokens last 15 minutes.
#   2. Remove the old test products first, or they will show up next to the new ones:
#      Atlas > Browse Collections > e-commerce-api > products > delete the old test documents.
#
# Same names, prices, colors, companies and categories as mockData/products.json, with these changes:
#   - "inventory" is added (the mock file has none, and our model requires it)
#   - the long lorem-ipsum descriptions are replaced by short ones, so the answers stay easy to read
#   - some products are "featured" and some have "freeShipping" (the mock file has neither)
# The inventory numbers are small on purpose. "albany sectional" has only 3 in stock, so in Part 6
# we can test "you ordered more than we have".
# (The categories are exactly as in the instructor's data: yes, the sofa is in "kitchen".)


### SEED1. accent chair -> 201, saves seedChairId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "accent chair",
  "price": 25999,
  "description": "A soft, comfortable chair for the office.",
  "category": "office",
  "company": "marcos",
  "colors": ["#ff0000", "#00ff00", "#0000ff"],
  "featured": true,
  "inventory": 10
}

> {%
    client.global.set('seedChairId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### SEED2. albany sectional -> 201, saves seedSectionalId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "albany sectional",
  "price": 109999,
  "description": "A large corner sofa with room for the whole family.",
  "category": "bedroom",
  "company": "liddy",
  "colors": ["#000", "#ffb900"],
  "freeShipping": true,
  "inventory": 3
}

> {%
    client.global.set('seedSectionalId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### SEED3. armchair -> 201, saves seedArmchairId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "armchair",
  "price": 12599,
  "description": "A small armchair that fits in any bedroom.",
  "category": "bedroom",
  "company": "marcos",
  "colors": ["#000", "#00ff00", "#0000ff"],
  "inventory": 25
}

> {%
    client.global.set('seedArmchairId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### SEED4. emperor bed -> 201, saves seedBedId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "emperor bed",
  "price": 23999,
  "description": "A wide bed with a strong wooden frame.",
  "category": "bedroom",
  "company": "ikea",
  "colors": ["#0000ff", "#000"],
  "featured": true,
  "freeShipping": true,
  "inventory": 7
}

> {%
    client.global.set('seedBedId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### SEED5. Read all products -> 200, "count": 4 (if you cleaned the old ones), newest first, no "image" yet
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products


### -------- IMAGES --------
# For now every product gets the same test photo. Later you can put your own pictures
# in the http folder and change the file names below.

### SEED6. Image for accent chair -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{seedChairId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="accent-chair.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../images/accent-chair.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### SEED7. Image for albany sectional -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{seedSectionalId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="albany-sectional.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../images/albany-sectional.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### SEED8. Image for armchair -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{seedArmchairId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="arm-chair.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../images/arm-chair.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### SEED9. Image for emperor bed -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{seedBedId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="emperor-bed.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../images/emperor-bed.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### SEED10. Read all products -> 200, all 4 have an "image" link
# Cloudinary > Assets > e-commerce-api/products: 4 files.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products
